# the keys are the scale: toggles, the root stays, three notes at least; modes and the root
wait 300
# the first piece is in Dorian; its root to C (Setup page, KNOB 1, down to its lowest)
expect par20 1
tap GLO
spin K1 -12
expect par19 0
tap HOME
# C Dorian: C D Eb F G A Bb. E4 is key 11: add E (relative 4)
expect pool 0x6AD
tapkey 11
expect pool 0x6BD
tapkey 11
expect pool 0x6AD
# key 7 is C4: the root stays
tapkey 7
expect pool 0x6AD
# the next mode: Phrygian
turn ALGO 1
expect par20 2
expect pool 0x5AB
turn ALGO -1
expect par20 1
expect pool 0x6AD
# the root up a tone: D Dorian (the pool is relative to the root: the same)
tap GLO
spin K1 2
expect par19 2
tap HOME
expect pool 0x6AD
wait 300
shot d_dorian.png
# pentatonic minor, then strip it down to three notes and try a fourth removal
turn ALGO 6
expect par20 7
expect pool 0x4A9
# D pent min: D F G A C. Remove F (key 0 = F3) and G (key 2 = G3)
tapkey 0
tapkey 2
expect pool 0x481
# A (key 4 = A3): would leave two
tapkey 4
expect pool 0x481
wait 300
shot three.png
# MIDI in, channel 1: G (note 55) back in
midi 90 37 64
wait 20
expect pool 0x4A1
expect dirty 1
